    "body": "There's plenty to not like with the resource selection algorithm and I share your wishlist. Here's how I think it should work overall, intended to match more closely how it's actually implemented: \r\n\r\n- A \"start resource selection\" algorithm that do only the steps before the first \"Await a stable state\"\r\n- Queue a microtask for the steps that follow up until \"End the synchronous section\" on each branch.\r\n- If _mode_ is _children_, set some state and use insertion/removal/move steps to react to changes.\r\n\r\nIn other words, no \"await a stable state\", no \"end the synchronous section\", no concept of a resource selection algorithm that's running and that can be aborted.\r\n\r\nI think it would be easier to make the whole change at once than building towards it over multiple PRs, but @nicolo-ribaudo let me know if you have no appetite for that and I can review this standalone.",
